REAL GAP, director-confirmed live (screenshot): Rules Generator's own report shows a summary like "16 rules, 9 after, 7 before, 1 couldn't be matched" -- but nowhere, even in the row's own expanded detail, does it say WHAT that 1 unmatched rule actually was. The count is the only trace of it; there's no way to act on it or even know which mod it involved.

ROOT CAUSE, confirmed via code read -- this is deeper than a UI rendering gap, the identity is discarded at the DATA layer: `lib/rules-generator.js`'s `computeMappingDetails` (~line 342-344):
```js
const rulesToConsider = copyable.map((r) => {
    if (!r.targetKey) {
      return { type: r.type, targetKey: null, status: 'unresolved' };
    }
```
When a rule's target can't be resolved to a real mod key at all, this throws away `r`'s own original target reference completely -- only `type` and the literal string `'unresolved'` survive. `web/public/rules-generator-app.js`'s own render (`rgRenderReadyCard`, ~line 187-197) then filters these out of the expanded detail table entirely (`resolvable = item.rulesToConsider.filter(r => r.status !== 'unresolved')`) -- even if the data DID survive, nothing renders it today either.

FIX, two parts:
1. **Preserve the original identity** at the point `status: 'unresolved'` is set -- `r` (the rule before this branch, from `resolvedCopyableRules`/the raw `ruleSet.rules` entry) still has its own `r.target` (the raw reference before `resolveRefToModKey` failed) -- keep that (or whatever human-readable form of it exists, e.g. `r.target`'s own name/reference field -- check `resolveRefToModKey`'s own input shape to know what's actually available to preserve) on the returned object instead of discarding it, so the UI has something real to show.
2. **Actually render it** -- add the unresolved rule(s) to the expanded detail view (`rgRenderReadyCard`'s `bodyHtml`), as their own clearly-distinct row/section (not mixed into the normal before/after/conflicts table, since there's no real rule TYPE decision to make here) -- something like "Couldn't match: a rule referencing '<original reference>' -- no mod in the old collection resolves to this, so it can't be copied." Casual register (informational, not consequential -- plain-language-writer).

VERIFY LIVE against a real collection pair that actually produces an unresolved rule (the director's own screenshot example, "Praedy's College of Winterhold 4K" copying from "Praedy's College of Winterhold 2K", 1 unresolved) -- confirm the expanded row now shows what that one rule actually was, not just the count. Handoff with what the real unresolved rule turned out to reference.
